    "text": "<p>Two dice <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are rolled. Let the numbers obtained on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> respectively. If the variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> are co-prime, then the sum of the positive divisors of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math> is equal to</p>",
